            <ArticleTitle>[Laughter therapy for chronic skeletal muscular pain].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>43-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors explain the effects introducing workshops for laughter therapy and relaxation to a unit dedicated to therapeutic education and functional rehabilitation; the authors test to see if the application of this therapy helps to decrease pain, to improve mobility and to reduce an altered emotional state, such as anxiety-depression, common among chronic pain patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
